      "text": "ICLR25 acceptances | Computing (https://computing.llnl.gov/about/newsroom/iclr25)\nciteturn6900view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://computing.llnl.gov/about/newsroom/iclr25\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 144\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * cite1†Our Purpose†www.llnl.gov L3:   * cite2†Our Science and Technology†www.llnl.gov L4:   * cite3†Join Our Team†www.llnl.gov L5:   * cite4†Partner with Us†www.llnl.gov L6:   * cite5†News†www.llnl.gov L7:   * cite6†Community and Education†www.llnl.gov L8:   * cite7†About†www.llnl.gov L9: \nL10: cite8†Computing L11: \nL12: April 14, 2025\nL13: # ICLR25 acceptances\nL14: \nL15: Join LLNL at the 13th International Conference on Learning Representations on April 24–28\nL16: \nL17: cite9†Image: Adobe Stock illustration of a brain shape made up of teal and pink filaments on an abstract background L18: Congratulations to the Livermore researchers whose work has been accepted to the 13th International Conference on Learning Representations (cite10†ICLR†iclr.cc ) on April 24–28 in Singapore. The event is known around the world for showcasing deep learning in artificial intelligence, statistics, and data science as well as a range of application areas. Follow LLNL Computing on X with the #ICLR25 hashtag. Workshop websites and preprints are linked below.\nL19: \nL20: * * *\nL21: Poster: cite11†ELFS: Label-Free Coreset Selection with Proxy Training Dynamics†arxiv.org | Brian Bartoldson, Bhavya Kailkhura\nL22: \nL23: Poster: cite12†Spectral-Refiner: Accurate Fine-Tuning of Spatiotemporal Fourier Neural Operator for Turbulent Flows†openreview.net | Ruipeng Li\nL24: \nL25: Workshop: cite13†Building Trust in Language Models and Applications†building-trust-in-llms.github.io L26: \nL27:   * AegisLLM: Scaling Agentic Systems for Self-Reflective Defense in LLM Security | Brian Bartoldson, Bhavya Kailkhura\nL28: